From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arvind Oruganti <aoruganti@microsoft.com>
Date: Wed, 1 Jul 2026 23:15:39 +0530
Subject: Fix ICU 78 CodeQL format-string warnings in cucdtst.c and cmsccoll.c

Clears the remaining cpp/wrong-type-format-argument (and one
cpp/tainted-format-string) alerts surfaced when the #153 restoration
touched these two files:
- cmsccoll.c: 22 UChar* printed with %s -> austrdup() (NUL-terminated) or
  aescstrdup(buf,len) (U16_APPEND / uset_getItem buffers).
- cucdtst.c: 59 %l* specifiers vs 32-bit args -> drop the l
  (%lx->%x, %lu->%u, %ld->%d); flagged specifier only.
- cucdtst.c MakeProp: log_err(str) -> log_err("%s", str) (tainted format).

Pre-existing upstream test-code issues; fixed per CodeQL guidance plus the
files own idioms. Implemented by GPT-5.5 (dual blind research), verified.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>

